  "id": "demonstration-experiment",
  "term": "demonstration experiment",
  "definition": "A demonstration experiment is a study in which participants are shown an ostensive demonstration of an action by a model, and researchers assess what parts of the demonstrated behavior, such as the means used or the goal, are later copied. In this packet, it refers to using demonstration and comparison conditions to study imitation and the interpretation of communicative intent in toddlers.",
